The paper’s central results are extremal existence theorems, not computational-hardness results. I’m checking the full proofs and cited regimes carefully because this distinction is decisive: generating a planted rainbow matching is easy, but it only qualifies if the generated distribution avoids the paper’s guaranteed/constructive easy regimes and rests on a defensible hard search problem.
