- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2011.04650/README.md)

The family asks for a full rainbow matching, represented as a perfect 3-partite matching. It is grounded in the [source paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.04650), with computational-hardness context from [Le and Pfender](https://arxiv.org/abs/1312.7253).

Results:

- All G1–G8 gates pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000.
- Three adversarial attacks: 0/8 each.
- Canonical key: 140 invariance checks and 120 carried-witness checks passed.
- Oracle verdict: `hardened` at `medium`, `n=32`, five choices per colour.
- Gemini and GPT-5.6 Terra returned invalid witnesses; Claude exhausted its 32,000-token response budget. Three Grok calls timed out and were correctly recorded as unscored errors.

No commit, push, or `submit.sh` operation was performed.
